      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Ten patients with symptomatic coronary artery disease received oral azithromycin for 3 days and underwent directional atherectomy on the third day. Azithromycin was found in all plaque samples with a median concentration of 284 ng/ml (95% confidence interval 163 to 517 ng/ml)."},
